{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional English ballad}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 3/4}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, ballad}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Are you going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair?
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
[Am]Remember [C]me to one who lives [G]there
[Am]For once she [G]was a true love of [Am]mine

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
[Am]Without no [C]seams nor needle[G]work
[Am]Then she'll be [G]a true love of [Am]mine

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Tell her to find me an [G]acre of [Am]land
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[D]mary and [Am]thyme
[Am]Between the [C]salt water and the sea [G]strands
[Am]Then she'll be [G]a true love of [Am]mine
